rom pelvic inflammatory disease as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "Borderline temperature and lack of lower abdominal pain weakly contradict PID as the septic shock source."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of jaundice and ascites in this chronic alcoholic with RUQ pain contradict Budd-Chiari syndrome as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "Absence of jaundice/ascites in a chronic alcoholic weakly contradicts Budd-Chiari syndrome."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's RUQ pain without lower abdominal symptoms or vaginal bleeding create a moderate inconsistency with gynecologic/pelvic pathology as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "The absence of vaginal bleeding, trauma history, or lower abdominal symptoms in this patient with RUQ pain and hemodynamic instability moderately weakens the broader gynecologic/pelvic pathology category (B1) as the primary diagnosis. However, ovarian torsion (B1.3) remains a weak_for possibility d…"}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of jaundice, ascites, and chronic liver disease findings in this chronic alcoholic with acute RUQ pain rule out Budd-Chiari syndrome as a dangerous alternative diagnosis?", "summary": "The absence of jaundice, ascites, and chronic liver disease findings in this chronic alcoholic with acute right upper quadrant pain weakly contradicts Budd-Chiari syndrome (hepatic vein thrombosis) as a dangerous alternative diagnosis. This finding does not appreciably support or weaken other branc…"}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.5], ["B2", 0.3], ["B2.1", 0.2]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.473], ["B1.3", 0.351], ["B2", 0.103]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.571], ["B1.3", 0.524], ["B2", 0.056]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "Patient exhibits hemodynamic instability (hypotension 80/40 mmHg, tachycardia 110 bpm) with severe localized right upper quadrant pain, meeting universal instability markers for shock or life-threatening abdominal process", "required_actions": ["Aggressive IV fluid bolus administration to address hypovolemic shock", "Immediate β-hCG result prioritization to rule out ruptured ectopic pregnancy", "Focused FAST ultrasound to detect intra-abdominal hemorrhage"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch (B1.3: Ovarian Torsion with Hemorrhage) has posterior=0.524 < 0.75. Dangerous alternatives (B1.1, B2.1) with posterior ≥ 0.03 remain unresolved. Tree depth=2 < max_depth=3. Available discriminators (FAST ultrasound, liver imaging, PID markers) can resolve uncertainty."}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.6, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.5242311323039514, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely the diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Ectopic implantation of a blastocyst"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Inflammation of the pancreas"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Obstruction of blood flow through the hepatic vein"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Obstruction of the common bile duct by radio-opaque stones"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Vascular ectasia within the liver"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Budd-Chiari syndrome', 'Biliary tract abnormality', 'Biliary cirrhosis', 'epigastric pain', 'gas', 'Lower abdominal pain', 'Biliary tract obstruction', 'pain'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "root_revision_needed": false, "program_faults": [], "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.441}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1.3", "label": "Ovarian Torsion with Hemorrhage", "posterior": 0.562, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0